  "namespaceProof": "r382 uses immutable r387 core package; production Core SHA matches final r393/r394/r397. Ordinary helpers in different observed Linux IPC namespaces reproduce extra IPC-only ceiling, refuse file-backed growth, and recover full capacity after actual parent death. No payload/resource/container/package qualification claimed.",
  "nativeStaging": "Generic RID apphost/native dependencies from r95, all managed DLL/PDB/JSON from terminal r395 harness build. Not a full publish/install/package qualification.",
  "nativeCaptureScope": "All3 inspected. Windows/Ubuntu owned windows; Mac authorized main display, unrelated content ignored and original local only. Scroll state deliberately positions captured link inspector/table. No physical-input/a11y qualification.",
  "rejectedCandidates": "r378 missing-token translation; r387/r390 Unix fixture shared flock conflicts with own exclusive lock; r391 Windows read-ahead overlaps initial lock byte. Production lock moved beyond EOF/read-ahead. Windows legacy IPC crash control now checks actual exit and polls same retained owner for kernel capacity retirement; no child/suite restart.",
  "publicSpillEnabled": false,
  "nativeInputQualified": false,
  "finalIndependentReviewPerformed": false,
  "remaining": [
